3. Avoid double-ticking on the contact simulation step

The current technique tracks sinceHit.

When contact happens, make sure the same fixed simulation step cannot produce:

immediate contact tick
+
scheduled 0.5-second tick

at once.

There should be exactly one tick on the contact step.

A clean state model would be something like:

this.nextTickAt = tickInterval;
this.immediateTickDue = true;

or equivalent.

When contact() succeeds:

queue exactly one immediate tick
sinceHit = 0
next normal tick occurs when sinceHit reaches 0.5

Do not depend on float equality.

Continue using the fixed-step simulation and threshold-crossing logic.

