14. Shield gameplay behavior

A successfully Shielded hit should be treated as blocked.

While Shield is active:

* melee attacks can be blocked;
* projectiles can be blocked;
* clone attacks can be blocked;
* charged-technique hits that are blockable can be blocked;
* the hit should not behave as a Dodge/pass-through;
* the attacking hit should still count as having connected with the Shield.

Preserve the existing Block semantics unless explicitly changed below.

The current project already has a Block-type path in CombatSystem, so replace #0001’s Dodge with that model and then change its Energy cost semantics.

⸻

15. Successful shielding costs 25 Energy

This is a major change from the current continuous Block drain.

Do not drain Energy just because the fighter is holding Shield.

Holding Shield with nobody attacking should cost:

0 Energy

A successful Shield against an attack costs exactly:

25 Energy

once per successfully blocked hit.

Examples:

100 → block hit → 75
75 → block hit → 50
50 → block hit → 25
25 → block hit → 0

This cost is triggered by the confirmed blocked hit event.

Do not charge 25:

* when Shield begins;
* every frame Shield is held;
* every second Shield is held;
* when an attack misses;
* when a projectile passes elsewhere;
* when the player taps Defense without being hit.

Only a successful Shield interaction costs it.

⸻

16. Define “successful Shield” precisely

A successful Shield means the shared hit resolver determines that:

target is currently shielding
+
the incoming hit would have struck the fighter
+
the hit resolves as a block

At that moment:

spendEnergy(25)

exactly once.

For an ordinary one-hit attack, one collision = one 25-point cost.

For a multihit technique/projectile, each separately resolved blocked hit can cost 25 if it is genuinely a separate hit event.

Do not consume multiple costs for the same hitbox on the same simulation step.

